    "result": "Great! The frai-core test suite is now fully passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Missing named exports in governance module** (`packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` and other constants as named exports from `./index.js`, but they were only available via the default export\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n**2. Toxicity metric signature mismatch** (`packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - The `toxicityMetric` function was accepting a second parameter `bannedTerms`, but when called from `runEvaluations`, it received `references` instead\n   - This caused the references (like `['hello', 'friendly world']`) to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging clean text as toxic\n   - Changed the function to only accept `outputs` and always use the hardcoded `defaultBannedTerms`\n\n## Test Results\n- **frai-core**: 8 test files, 28 tests \u2713 passing\n- **frai-gate**: 1 test file, 11 tests \u2713 passing\n- **Total**: 39 tests \u2713 passing\n\nAll existing public exports remain intact and functional.",
